;; The AOT's side of the runtime (PY8; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md §7, PYS13 (a); doc/python/PYI-SPEC.md
;; §10): arbace.python.aot translates each code object's IR into a Go function over this package, a
;; compiled interpreter: the instructions become Go statements calling the helpers below with their
;; arguments as constants, the jumps gotos, the decoding and the dispatch loop's switch gone. The
;; frame stays the machine's heap frame (its stack, locals, cells, PC and Lasti), so a compiled
;; function is run by the same loop (Thread.run) in place of step: a call of a Python function still
;; pushes the callee's frame (the Go stack never holds Python frames, RecursionError where CPython
;; raises it), an exception unwinds by the code's exception table, and a generator's or coroutine's
;; frame is resumed by the function's entry switch on its PC (a state machine over the heap frame).
;;
;; A compiled program registers its modules' IR (the loader's text) with their native functions in
;; pre-order (the code object, then its nested code objects in constant order); the loader attaches
;; them (ReadIR's irLoadedHook). Source compiled at run time (exec, eval, compile, an import of a module
;; not compiled ahead) goes to the host's compiler (PYI_AOT_COMPILER, arbace.python.aot compile-server)
;; and runs on the dispatch loop.

